WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:02.190
- [Narrator] If you doubled in size,

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:05.173
your weight would be eight times greater.

00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:08.780
That's the trouble with growing tall.

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:11.620
Gravity's pull is keeping us all down,

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:13.680
but there are a few earthly giants

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.635
that have fought gravity and won.

00:00:16.635 --> 00:00:20.220
(gentle instrumental music)

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.203
The key to growing tall is
how you use your energy.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:28.840
That's why the tallest trees
outrank any animal on Earth,

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.853
because trees spend all
their energy on one thing;

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.993
growing taller than
their fellow neighbors.

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:38.450
And there are two trees
that are the best growers

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:43.200
of them all: giant redwoods
and mountain ashes.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:46.603
Redwoods are renowned as the
tallest lifeforms on Earth,

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:51.010
but some experts think that
mountain ashes could grow

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:55.173
even taller if humans would
stop cutting them down.

00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:59.760
In fact, the tallest mountain ash was just

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.223
one meter shorter than
the tallest redwood.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:07.530
Unlike plants, animals spend
energy on all sorts of tasks,

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:11.530
like eating, walking, and staying warm,

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:13.053
so they can't grow as tall.

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:16.410
But it doesn't mean they're small, either.

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:19.360
If you measured this African elephant

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:21.270
from shoulder to ground,

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:24.210
it would actually be
taller than a giraffe,

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:26.220
but thanks to their long, strong necks,

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:28.453
giraffes are the tallest animals alive.

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:33.190
And if we look at animals
throughout Earth's history,

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:35.113
dinosaurs eclipsed them all.

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:39.223
These towering sauropods were
the biggest of the bunch.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:42.770
In fact, the top ten lists of tallest

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:45.743
animals in history? All dinosaurs.

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:50.453
But what if we looked at
the longest lifeforms, too?

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:56.023
If you balance the longest
saltwater crocodile on its nose,

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:58.703
it would tie the giraffe.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:02.593
And if we ignore legs it gets even better.

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:06.180
Tip-to-tail, the green
anaconda nearly doubles

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:07.993
the height of the tallest giraffe.

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:14.560
But these land-dwellers have
nothing on animals of the deep.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:18.430
Supported by water, sea life
can practically ignore gravity,

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:20.873
which means they can grow much larger.

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:24.740
Take the blue whale, for example.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:28.120
It's the most massive animal of all time.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:30.650
For example, the entire cast of Broadway's

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:34.183
The Lion King can fit on its tongue.

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:38.100
But it should be careful
not to get tangled up

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:40.773
in the tentacles of a
lion's mane jellyfish,

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:45.083
which makes the giant squid
look small by comparison.

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:49.820
Now, the biggest fish
alive is the whale shark,

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:52.923
and if we look into the
past things get even bigger.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:56.123
So where do humans fit into all this?

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:59.343
Somewhere near the top, actually.

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:04.750
Humans are bigger than
87.6% of mammals on Earth

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:08.440
and the average Dutchman
is the tallest of them all.

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:12.080
So there's no reason to
ever feel small again,

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:14.618
especially if you're from the Netherlands.

00:03:14.618 --> 00:03:16.550
(gentle instrumental music)

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:19.630
Fun fact, the longest
life-form of all time

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:21.910
isn't a plant or animal at all.

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:24.940
It's a honey fungus and
the biggest one goes on

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:28.783
for 3.8 kilometers underneath
a forest in Oregon.

